'''''Festuca paniculata''''' (east Alpine violet fescue) is a grass with culms 60–120&nbsp;cm long, endemic to central, southwestern, and southeastern [[Europe]] and northern [[Africa]]. It was first described in 1913.<ref name = powo>{{cite web |title=''Festuca burnatii'' St.-Yves |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:402485-1? |website=Festuca burnatii St.-Yves |access-date=10 May 2023}}</ref>


